const readingExplanations = {
  17: [
    [
      [16,"In the first half of the 1800s, London’s population ","grew at an astonishing rate",", and the central area became increasingly congested.","题目把 the first half of the 1800s 写成 1800–1850，把 grew at an astonishing rate 写成 increased rapidly。增长的主语是 London’s population，后面的交通拥堵是结果。"],
      [16,"His idea was to relocate the poor workers who lived in the inner-city slums ","to newly constructed suburbs",", and to provide cheap rail travel for them to get to work.","Pearson 想把住在市内贫民窟的工人迁到新建郊区，并给他们便宜的交通。题目问迁往哪里，填 suburbs；workers 是搬迁的人。"],
      [16,"Pearson’s ideas ","gained support amongst some businessmen"," and in 1851 he submitted a plan to Parliament.","agreed with Pearson’s idea 对应 gained support。提供支持的人是 businessmen，后文通过议案的 Parliament 不是题目所问。"],
      [16,"The organisation had ","difficulty in raising the funding"," for such a radical and expensive scheme, not least because of the critical articles printed by the press.","had problems getting 与 had difficulty in raising 对应。所筹集的是 funding；下一段的 £250,000 是出资额，不能替代资金这个名词。"],
      [16,"The organisation had difficulty in raising the funding for such a radical and expensive scheme, not least because of the ","critical articles printed by the press",".","negative articles 对应 critical articles。题干问文章在哪出现，printed by the press 直接定位到 press，不填提出反对意见的人。"],
      [17,"","A two-metre-deep layer of soil"," was laid on top of the tunnel and the road above rebuilt.","brick arch 建完形成隧道，接着在顶部覆盖厚土。题干问覆盖材料，填 soil；砖是拱本身的材料，木梁早先用于支撑。"],
      [17,"The Metropolitan line, which opened on 10 January 1863, was ","the world’s first underground railway",".","大都会线被明确称为世界第一条地下铁路，不可能已有他国的地下铁路先开通。题干与 first 直接冲突，判 FALSE。"],
      [17,"","On its first day, almost 40,000"," passengers were carried between Paddington and Farringdon, the journey taking about 18 minutes.","首日实载近 40,000 人，但题干说超过事前预估。文中没有预计数，不能用 18 分钟车程或全年 950 万人次来比较，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [17,"However, ","smoke and fumes remained a problem",", even though ventilation shafts were added to the tunnels.","even though 引出虽然加了通风井却仍有烟气，正对应未能防止隧道污染。题目问措施效果，不是说根本没有通风。"],
      [17,"","The only alternative was to tunnel deep underground",".","中心区域不能用 cut and cover，唯一可行方式是深挖隧道。这正是 a different approach was required，判 TRUE。"],
      [17,"The carriages were narrow and had ","tiny windows just below the roof"," because it was thought that passengers would not want to look out at the tunnel walls.","窗子紧靠车顶下方；设计者以为乘客不想看隧道壁。题干说窗在眼睛高度，位置与原文矛盾。"],
      [17,"Although the City & South London Railway was a great technical achievement, ","it did not make a profit",".","作者先肯定技术成就，再说没盈利。financial success 必须看财务结果，不能把技术成功当成盈利，判 FALSE。"],
      [17,"","It was very popular"," and soon afterwards new railways and extensions were added to the growing tube network.","末段给出 Tuppenny Tube 的电动机车、受欢迎程度与后续扩建，没有发车或到站准点数据。popular 不等于 punctual，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [20,"Today, however, stadiums are ","regarded with growing scepticism",".","A 段先回顾体育场的历史，再用 however 转到当今的质疑，列出成本高与赛后闲置。搜索 negative attitudes 时可对应 scepticism。"],
      [21,"This ","reduces the annual output of carbon dioxide by 660 tons"," and supplies up to 80 percent of the surrounding area when the stadium is not in use.","F 段用高雄体育场的 8,844 块光伏板、年发电和减排数据证明环境收益。题目要求具体 figures；E 段虽讲土地效率，但不给这些数字。"],
      [21,"There’s a growing trend for stadiums to be equipped with public spaces and services that serve a function beyond sport, such as ","hotels, retail outlets, conference centres",", restaurants and bars, children’s playgrounds and green space.","E 段列酒店、零售、会议、餐饮、游乐和绿地，几个类别共同体现 wide range。F 段讲的是可再生能源设备，不是公共服务清单。"],
      [21,"… space surrounded by tiers of seats for spectators, for the presentation of dramatic or sporting events Many such stadiums are situated in suburban areas, ","designed for sporting use only"," and surrounded by parking lots.","D 段先标定二十世纪，再说地点在郊区、用途单一、耗能并加剧热岛。题目所找的是那一时期的缺点，不能选描述今天改进的 E 段。"],
      [20,"Built by the Romans in 90 AD, ","it became a fortress"," with four towers after the fifth century, and was then transformed into a village containing more than 200 houses.","B 段的时间顺序是罗马建成后先作堡垒，再成有两百余栋房子的村落。题目要求首次改用途，填 fortress。"],
      [20,"With the growing interest in conservation during the 19th century, it was converted back into an arena for ","the staging of bullfights",", thereby returning the structure to its original use as a venue for public spectacles.","Arles 经过保护修复变回表演场地，举办斗牛。staging 对应 spectators could watch；不要拿下一句 Verona 的 opera 来填。"],
      [20,"It has endured the centuries and is currently considered one of the world’s ","prime sites for opera",", thanks to its outstanding acoustics.","修饰地点的是 Verona，时间词 currently 对应 today。优秀的 acoustics 解释它适合歌剧，空格问上演什么。"],
      [20,"The site evolved in a similar way to Arles and was progressively filled with buildings from the Middle Ages until the 19th century, variously used as houses, ","a salt depot"," and a prison.","Lucca 的遗址先后用作民居、盐仓和监狱。storage of 改写 depot 的功能，空格填储存物 salt。"],
      [20,"Today, the ruins of the amphitheatre remain embedded in the ","various shops and residences"," surrounding the public square.","遗址嵌在广场周围的商铺和住宅里。题干已给 homes 对应 residences，补上并列的 shops。"],
      [21,"These factors mean that ","they may not be as accessible"," to the general public, require more energy to run and contribute to urban heat.","C。D 段说明许多二十世纪体育场位于郊区，公众不易到达，对应位置不便。该双选 C、D 顺序不限。"],
      [20,"But ","some of the flexibility was lost"," at the beginning of the 20th century, as stadiums were developed using new products such as steel and reinforced concrete, and made use of bright lights …","D。D 段随后用 designed for sporting use only 解释灵活性下降，对应用途更单一。钢和混凝土是材料背景，不表示更不耐用。"],
      [21,"Creating mixed-use developments such as this reinforces compactness and multi-functionality, making more efficient use of land and ","helping to regenerate urban spaces",".","B。E 段的商店、公共空间和游乐场引入家庭与更广泛人群，让城市区域重新活跃。重点是社区使用，不是改善观赛设施。"],
      [21,"Stadiums are ideal for these purposes, because their canopies have a ","large surface area for fitting photovoltaic panels"," and rise high enough (more than 40 metres) to make use of micro wind turbines.","E。F 段说顶棚面积大能装光伏，高度够还能用小风机。这解释体育场适合安装装置；给居民供电不同于让居民减少用电。"],
      [24,"After his father was executed by the Parliamentarians in 1649, the young Charles II sacrificed one of the very principles his father had died for and ","did a deal with the Scots",", thereby accepting Presbyterianism* as the national religion in return for being crowned King of Scots.","H。与苏格兰人达成交易以换取王位，是政治上的结盟。前文对宗教信仰的让步是这项交易的条件，不是空格所问的联盟本身。"],
      [24,"After his father was executed by the Parliamentarians in 1649, the young Charles II sacrificed one of the very principles his father had died for and did a deal with the Scots, ","thereby accepting Presbyterianism","* as the national religion in return for being crowned King of Scots.","J。为获苏格兰王位，Charles 接受长老宗，放弃父亲为之而死的原则。题干问放弃原则的性质，religious conviction 对应宗教信念。"],
      [24,"After being ","comprehensively defeated"," on the meadows outside the city by the Parliamentarian army, the 21-year-old king found himself the subject of a national manhunt, with a huge sum offered …","F。原文从 Charles 一方说惨败，题干从 Parliamentarians 一方说获胜。comprehensively 说明胜负明确，所以是 decisive victory。"],
      [24,"After being comprehensively defeated on the meadows outside the city by the Parliamentarian army, the 21-year-old king found himself the subject of a national manhunt, with ","a huge sum"," offered for his capture.","B。offered for his capture 表明钱是悬赏，huge sum 对应 large reward。不要把开价对象误解为逃跑途中带的钱。"],
      [24,"Over the following six weeks he managed, through a series of heart-poundingly close escapes, to evade the Parliamentarians before ","seeking refuge in France",".","D。六周后在法国避难，对应抵达欧陆相对安全处。relative 很重要；贵族仍失势且缺钱，不能推断从此绝对安全。"],
      [24,"His intention when asking Pepys to commit his story to paper was to ","ensure that this most extraordinary episode was never forgotten",".","书评交代请 Pepys 落笔是为了保存逃亡故事，但不解释为什么挑中这个人。是否认为 Pepys 值得信任无法推断，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [24,"Over two three-hour sittings, the king related to him ","in great detail"," his personal recollections of the six weeks he had spent as a fugitive.","两次各三小时，国王向 Pepys 详细回忆六周经历。in great detail 与 lacked sufficient detail 相反，判 NO。"],
      [24,"As the king and secretary settled down (a scene that is surely a gift for a future scriptwriter), Charles commenced his story: ‘","After the battle was so absolutely lost"," as to be beyond hope of recovery, I began to think of the best way of saving myself.’","Charles 自述战局彻底失败后才开始想怎么自救。题干把制定计划的时点提前到战前，判 NO。"],
      [24,"One of the joys of Spencer’s book, a result not least of ","its use of Charles II’s own narrative"," as well as those of his supporters, is just how close the reader gets to the action.","书评把使用本人叙述列为读者贴近事件的一大乐趣。one of the joys 指明作者确实把它当优点，判 YES。"],
      [24,"Charles Spencer’s latest book, To Catch a King, tells us the story of the hunt for King Charles II ","in the six weeks after his resounding defeat"," at the Battle of Worcester in September 1651.","B。首段交代弑君、与苏格兰结盟、战败、遭悬赏直至逃亡的前因。战斗本身没有细写，政治与宗教也服务于背景叙述。"],
      [24,"One of the joys of Spencer’s book, a result not least of its use of Charles II’s own narrative as well as those of his supporters, is ","just how close the reader gets to the action",".","C。剪发、染皮肤和躲在树上这些细节让读者如临现场。个别场景危险，但举例整体强调六周经历被写得鲜活。"],
      [25,"It is hard to imagine many other kings ","marking the lowest point in their life so enthusiastically",", or indeed pulling off such an escape in the first place.","A。逃亡源于失败，却被 Charles 用骑士勋位、绘画等纪念。lowest point 与 enthusiastically 的对照是书评观点。"],
      [25,"He has ","even-handed sympathy"," for both the fugitive king and the fierce republican regime that hunted him, and he succeeds in his desire to explore far more of the background of the …","B。评论说 Spencer 对逃亡的国王与追捕他的共和政权都抱有同等理解。even-handed 等于不偏不倚，不能据现代用语那句推出 D。"],
      [25,"","Would Charles II have been a different king"," had these six weeks never happened?","D。书评追问六周逃亡有没有塑造后来的国王，认为书中晚年形象没回答这种长期影响。伪装和计谋已经提到，并非漏写。"]
    ],
    [
      [37,"","One of these young shepherds tossed a rock"," into an opening on the side of a cliff and was surprised to hear a shattering sound.","threw 对应 tossed；he 听到碎裂声。题目要被扔进去的物体，a 后填 rock，不填响声 sound。"],
      [37,"He and his companions ","later entered the cave"," and stumbled across a collection of large clay jars, seven of which contained scrolls with writing on them.","开头的 opening 是悬崖上的入口，少年随后实际走进 cave 并找到罐子。went into 等于 entered。"],
      [37,"He and his companions later entered the cave and stumbled across ","a collection of large clay jars",", seven of which contained scrolls with writing on them.","containers 泛指 jars，made of 要填材料 clay。不是写容器名称，也不是写罐内的卷轴。"],
      [37,"The area was known as Judea at that time, and the people are thought to have belonged to ","a group called the Essenes",", a devout Jewish sect.","属主流学说但仍有争论。人群所属派别名 Essenes 对应 known as；Judea 是地区名，Jewish 只是描述。"],
      [37,"","The majority of the texts on the Dead Sea Scrolls are in Hebrew",", with some fragments written in an ancient version of its alphabet thought to have fallen out of use in the fifth century BCE.","mainly 对应 majority，填 Hebrew。Aramaic 和 Greek 都出现过，但并非主要文字。"],
      [37,"The teenagers took the seven scrolls to a nearby town where they were ","sold for a small sum"," to a local antiquities dealer.","原文只说卖价低，没有说少年情绪如何。低价不足以推断他们失望，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [37,"The origin of the Dead Sea Scrolls, which were written around 2,000 years ago between 150 BCE and 70 CE, is ","still the subject of scholarly debate"," even today.","scholarly debate 表明仍在争论，直接反驳 academics agree。prevailing theory 只说某学说流行，并非大家一致。"],
      [37,"","The only entire book"," of the Hebrew Bible preserved among the manuscripts from Qumran is Isaiah; this copy, dated to the first century BCE, is considered the earliest biblical …","只有《以赛亚书》保存完整，其他经卷保存为 fragments。only one complete 支持多数不完整，判 TRUE。"],
      [38,"Using ","an unconventional vocabulary and odd spelling",", it describes 64 underground hiding places that supposedly contain riches buried for safekeeping.","unconventional 与 odd 表明用词拼法不同寻常，正对应 unusual way。题干关注记录方式，不是问藏宝地点有没有找到。"],
      [38,"In 1948, a Syrian Orthodox archbishop known as Mar Samuel acquired four of the original seven scrolls from a Jerusalem shoemaker and part-time antiquity dealer, ","paying less than $100 for them",".","Mar Samuel 从商人手中买走四卷，有明确付款，题干说收到赠礼，判 FALSE。广告里说可当礼物是后来招徕买家。"],
      [38,"He then travelled to the United States and ","unsuccessfully offered them"," to a number of universities, including Yale.","他向包括耶鲁在内的大学推销未果，随后才登报。题干称多机构 keen to buy，与这段叙述相反，判 FALSE。"],
      [38,"The scroll names celebrations that indicate shifts in seasons and details ","two yearly religious events"," known from another Dead Sea Scroll.","2017 年拼合的卷轴记录季节庆典及每年宗教活动。yearly 对应 annual，题干说的正是这类活动，判 TRUE。"],
      [38,"Only ","one more known scroll remains untranslated",".","末段给出两位海法大学研究者解译了此前一卷，仍有末卷未译。未交代现在是否由该校继续研究，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [42,"In this way they managed to create a strain ","resistant to a common disease"," called bacterial spot race, which can devastate yields.","C 段讲中国团队得到抗细菌性病害的品系，病害可令产量严重受损。这对应 resist a dangerous infection。"],
      [41,"But every time a single plant with a mutation is taken from a larger population for breeding, ","much genetic diversity is lost",".","B 段强调反复从群体里只挑一株育种会丢失遗传多样性，而且有利性状可能伴有不利性状。题目要限制选择为何产生问题。"],
      [42,"The three teams already have their eye on other plants that could be ‘","catapulted into the mainstream","’, including foxtail, oat-grass and cowpea.","E 段举 foxtail、oat-grass、cowpea 等可推广的例子。题目找例子清单，而 D 段的主要对象只有 groundcherry。"],
      [41,"Now two separate teams in Brazil and China have done it all over again ","in less than three years",".","A 段将过去用至少 3,000 年驯化与巴西、中国不到三年重做相对照。两个时间尺度对应 early 与 recent。"],
      [42,"‘","They are quite tasty",",’ says Kudla.","C 段 Kudla 亲自评价味道浓、芳香。题目问个人品尝反应，B 段谈超市番茄风味流失是一般现象。"],
      [42,"By choosing wild plants that are ","drought or heat tolerant",", says Gao, we could create crops that will thrive even as the planet warms.","B 是 Gao。她把耐旱和耐热的野生植物与未来气候变暖联系起来，对应 adapt to future environmental challenges。"],
      [42,"But it will be ","hard for new foods to grow so popular"," with farmers and consumers that they become new staple crops, he thinks.","D 是 Jones。他怀疑冷门食物能否被农民与消费者普遍接受并成为主粮，正对应 may not be accepted on a large scale。"],
      [42,"But Kudla ","didn’t want to reveal which species"," were in his team’s sights, because CRISPR has made the process so easy.","A 是 Kudla。未来想研究哪些物种，他选择不公开，因为其他有相应能力的人也能开展。题干说的是研究方向的保密。"],
      [42,"But she adds that ","taking the work further would be expensive"," because of the need to pay for a licence for the CRISPR technology and get regulatory approval.","C 是 Van Eck。她说继续开发 groundcherry 的授权和审批需要钱，正是成本限制了后续工作。"],
      [41,"‘There are 50,000 edible plants in the world, but ","90 percent of our energy comes from just 15 crops",".’","A 是 Kudla。他把地球上约 5 万种可食植物与提供九成能量的 15 种作物相比，说明我们实际靠的食物来源很窄。"],
      [41,"For instance, the tomato strains grown for supermarkets have ","lost much of their flavour",".","题干已写 loss of，后面需要不利性状的名词。B 段举超市番茄风味流失为例，填 flavour 或 flavor。"],
      [42,"For instance, they ","tripled the size of fruit"," by editing a gene called FRUIT WEIGHT, and increased the number of tomatoes per truss by editing another called MULTIFLORA.","tripled 对应 three times，空格在 its original 后要名词 size。文中随后说每串果实数量增加，是另一项变化。"],
      [42,"They also created another strain that is ","more salt tolerant"," – and has higher levels of vitamin C.","not badly affected by 对应 tolerant。维生素 C 较高与耐盐出现在同一个品系，不能换成前一句的细菌性病害。"],
      [45,"","Scientific discovery is popularly believed"," to result from the sheer genius of such intellectual stars as naturalist Charles Darwin and theoretical physicist Albert Einstein.","D。首段概述大众把发现归功于天才和突然灵感的假设，下一段才批评它。题目只问首段功能。"],
      [45,"However, we believe that it ","largely misrepresents the real nature"," of scientific discovery, as well as that of creativity and innovation in many other realms of human endeavor.","A。作者承认旧看法或许有限正确，但指出它大体歪曲发现的性质，属批评观点。随后段落才详谈替代框架。"],
      [45,"","Setting aside such greats as Darwin and Einstein"," – whose monumental contributions are duly celebrated – we suggest that innovation is more a process of trial and error, where two steps forward may sometimes …","A。把这两位伟大人物先放在一边，作者转谈创新通常是试错积累，说明他们被当作这个一般规律讨论之外的特例。"],
      [45,"Niels Bohr, the Nobel prize-winning father of modern atomic theory, ","jumped off from this interesting idea"," to conceive his now-famous model of the atom.","C。Nicholson 的某些推测错了，但原子结构的新想法成了 Bohr 建立自身模型的出发点。题目问为谁的突破铺垫。"],
      [46,"","He suffered a leg injury",", which left him unable to fully bend his left knee.","A。Westrope 为了弯不了左膝才改马镫，转弯更快是意外。普及很快属结果，题干问发明有趣之处，抓起因。"],
      [46,"These notions ","merely label rather than explain"," the evolution of human innovations.","贴上「天才」的标签并没有说明创意怎样出现。题干说这个称呼有助理解创造过程，被作者直接反驳，判 NO。"],
      [46,"","The Law of Effect was advanced"," by psychologist Edward Thorndike in 1898, some 40 years after Charles Darwin published his groundbreaking work on biological evolution, On the Origin of Species.","作者给 Thorndike 提出法则的 1898 年与达尔文著作的时间差，没有交代那个时代心理学家当时在找创意起因，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [46,"Just like Darwin’s Law of Natural Selection, the Law of Effect involves an entirely mechanical process of variation and selection, ","without any end objective in sight",".","文中强调变异和筛选没有预设终点，成功行为才被重复。题干的 no planning 与该机械过程一致，判 YES。"],
      [46,"In particular, the provenance of the raw material on which the Law of Effect operates ","is not as clearly known"," as that of the genetic mutations on which the Law of Natural Selection operates.","作者说新想法和行为的来源仍不够清楚，可能受既有成败限制。题干说已经有清楚解释，判 NO。"],
      [46,"","The time seems right for abandoning"," the naive notions of intelligent design and genius, and for scientifically exploring the true origins of creative behavior.","这是作者呼吁现在放弃旧观念。文章没提供科学家已经转变的人数或趋势，不能把倡议等同现实观察，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [45,"Conventional wisdom also places great weight on insight in promoting breakthrough scientific achievements, as if ","ideas spontaneously pop into someone’s head"," – fully formed and functional.","F。突然蹦入脑中、而且完全成形的想法，就是 sudden inspiration。invention 是后来的成果，和灵感不是一回事。"],
      [45,"These successes are all the more noteworthy given the fact that Nicholson was wrong about the presence of proto-elements: ","they do not actually exist",".","D。Nicholson 假定的原始元素根本不存在，这个例子说明错误也可能给后来发现提供材料。"],
      [46,"Plenty of other stories show that fresh advances can arise from error, misadventure, and also pure ","serendipity – a happy accident",".","E。两名员工各有难题，弱胶和临时书签恰好拼成便利贴。这种偶然巧合是 luck，并非事前实验的计划。"],
      [46,"Just like Darwin’s Law of Natural Selection, the Law of Effect involves an entirely ","mechanical process of variation and selection",", without any end objective in sight.","B。两个法则共同点是变异与筛选，不要求预设终点。题干 no clear 对应 without any end objective，选 goals。"]
    ],
    [
      [59,"In terms of feeding, ","it was exclusively carnivorous",", and its stomach was muscular with an ability to distend so that it could eat large amounts of food at one time, probably an adaptation to compensate …","entirely 对应 exclusively。diet 前缺描述食性的形容词，填 carnivorous；下面描述胃能扩张是另一个特征。"],
      [59,"During long-distance chases, thylacines were likely to have ","relied more on scent than any other sense",".","relied more on 对应 depended mainly on，指追猎时主要靠嗅觉。题目问所用的感官，填 scent，不填捕猎时段。"],
      [59,"","Newborns crawled into the pouch"," on the belly of their mother, and attached themselves to one of the four teats, remaining there for up to three months.","初生幼崽进母亲腹部育儿袋，留到最多三个月，吻合 first months。lair 是离开袋后待的巢穴。"],
      [59,"The most recent, well-dated occurrence of a thylacine on the mainland is ","a carbon-dated fossil"," from Murray Cave in Western Australia, which is around 3,100 years old.","最近一件有可靠年代的澳大利亚大陆证据，是 Murray Cave 约 3,100 年前的化石。cave 是发现地，fossil 是证据本身。"],
      [60,"These include competition with wild dogs introduced by European settlers, ","loss of habitat along with the disappearance of prey species",", and a distemper-like disease which may also have affected the thylacine.","reduction 对应 loss，available sources of food 对应 prey species。空格是与食物减少并列的 habitat。"],
      [60,"… the mother’s belly The dramatic decline of the thylacine in Tasmania, which began in the 1830s and continued for a century, is generally attributed to ","the relentless efforts of sheep farmers and bounty hunters","** with shotguns.","原文把从 1830 年代开始并延续百年的大幅衰减主要归于牧农和赏金猎人的枪杀，支持从此时起大量被人杀死。其他原因也存在。"],
      [60,"There was ","only one successful attempt to breed"," a thylacine in captivity, at Melbourne Zoo in 1899.","只有墨尔本动物园在 1899 年有一次成功的圈养繁殖。经过伦敦等动物园的动物数量多，不能等同出生多；题干说 several，判 FALSE。"],
      [60,"The famous naturalist ","John Gould foresaw the thylacine’s demise"," when he published his Mammals of Australia between 1848 and 1863, writing, ‘The numbers of this singular animal will speedily diminish, extermination …","原文给出 Gould 对袋狼灭绝的预测，没有说明任何生物学家听到后是否吃惊。不能从预测正确推断听众反应，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [60,"However, there seems to have been little public pressure to preserve the thylacine, ","nor was much concern expressed by scientists"," at the decline of this species in the decades that followed.","作者明确说科学家并未表现出多少关切，并将 Flynn 作为例外。与 many scientists became worried 相反，判 FALSE。"],
      [60,"In 1914, he was sufficiently concerned about the scarcity of the thylacine to suggest that some should be captured and ","placed on a small island",".","Flynn 建议捕捉一些放到小岛，原文未报告尝试或可行性结论。只看到提议不等于已证明不现实，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [60,"But it was not until 1929, with the species ","on the very edge of extinction",", that Tasmania’s Animals and Birds Protection Board passed a motion protecting thylacines only for the month of December, which was thought to be their …","1929 年通过繁殖季保护动议时，袋狼已在灭绝边缘。reasonable numbers 与这个数量状态矛盾。"],
      [60,"The last known wild thylacine to be killed was shot by a farmer in the north-east of Tasmania in 1930, ","leaving just captive specimens",".","1930 年最后一只已知野生袋狼被射杀，之后只剩圈养个体，1936 年最后一只死于动物园。两个边界年份都能对上。"],
      [60,"There have been ","numerous expeditions and searches"," for the thylacine over the years, none of which has produced definitive evidence that thylacines still exist.","原文说历年有多次搜寻且无确凿证据，未比较近日和过去的搜寻频率。rarely now 既不能确认也不能否定。"],
      [64,"That immensely high yield – which is predominantly what makes it so profitable – is ","potentially also an ecological benefit",".","F 段先从高单位产量推少占土地，再讨论相对于某些作物的固碳优势。题干用 potential，因环境收益取决于替代的地类。"],
      [64,"G ","The industry is now regulated"," by a group called the Roundtable on Sustainable Palm Oil (RSPO), consisting of palm growers, retailers, product manufacturers, and other interested parties.","G 段介绍 RSPO 的成员、认证条件和认证产量。禁止清原始森林等条件体现它控制环境影响的方式。"],
      [63,"It’s almost certainly in ","the soap we wash with"," in the morning, the sandwich we have for lunch, and the biscuits we snack on during the day.","A 段说这是全球消费最多的植物油，接着举肥皂、三明治、饼干例示用途之广。B 段数字说的是产量和面积增长。"],
      [64,"","The bird’s nest fern"," (Asplenium nidus) grows on trees in an epiphytic fashion (meaning it’s dependent on the tree only for support, not for nutrients), and is native to many …","H 段认为鸟巢蕨可以给多类生物提供栖所，可能帮种植园恢复生态。特指能改善生态的一种生物。"],
      [63,"Between 1990 and 2012, the global land area devoted to growing oil palm trees ","grew from 6 to 17 million hectares",", now accounting for around ten percent of total cropland in the entire world.","B 段给出 1990–2012 年面积变化及年产量由约 200 万到 6,000 万吨的数据，支持 rapid expansion。G 段只统计认证规模。"],
      [64,"Is it desirable to have palm oil boycotted, replaced, eliminated from the global supply chain, given how many low-income people in developing countries ","depend on it for their livelihoods","?","E 段反对全面抵制的经济理由是众多低收入者靠它谋生、摆脱贫困。不能只看 D 段提出的抵制问题。"],
      [63,"Endangered species – most famously the Sumatran orangutan, but also ","rhinos, elephants, tigers",", and numerous other fauna – have suffered from the unstoppable spread of oil palm plantations.","C 段列红毛猩猩、犀牛、大象和老虎等受森林清理及栖息地破坏影响的动物。H 段列的是有望受益的生物。"],
      [64,"The RSPO insists upon ","no virgin forest clearing, transparency"," and regular assessment of carbon stocks, among other criteria.","B。认证要求 transparency，对应公开、诚实披露做法。文中没有与其他行业监管严格度比较。这组 B、C 不限顺序。"],
      [64,"Over the past decade or so, an ","agreement has gradually been reached"," regarding standards that producers of palm oil have to meet in order for their product to be regarded as officially ‘sustainable’.","C。标准是在过去约十年逐步达成的，涵盖 several years。该时间修饰制定标准，未说会员持续增加。"],
      [63,"Primarily because its unique properties – such as ","remaining solid at room temperature"," – make it an ideal ingredient for long-term preservation, allowing many packaged foods on supermarket shelves to have ‘best before’ dates of months, even …","even when not refrigerated 对应 at room temperature；stays 对应 remaining。空格用形容词 solid。"],
      [63,"Endangered species – ","most famously the Sumatran orangutan",", but also rhinos, elephants, tigers, and numerous other fauna – have suffered from the unstoppable spread of oil palm plantations.","best known 对应 most famously，锁定受栖息地破坏影响的猩猩。在不超过两词的要求下可填 Sumatran orangutan。"],
      [64,"The RSPO insists upon no virgin forest clearing, transparency and ","regular assessment of carbon stocks",", among other criteria.","check ... on a routine basis 改写 regular assessment。原文要求定期评估的是 carbon stocks，禁止清林是并列条件。"],
      [64,"Ellwood believes that reintroducing the bird’s nest fern into oil palm plantations could potentially allow these areas to ","recover their biodiversity",", providing a home for all manner of species, from fungi and bacteria, to invertebrates such as insects, amphibians, reptiles and even mammals.","restore 对应 recover。H 段解释鸟巢蕨为多类生物提供家园，空格是要恢复的 biodiversity。"],
      [67,"The book ","combines geology, history, economics",", and a lot of data to explain why business clusters developed where they did and how the early decisions of workers and firms shaped the skyline we see today.","D。首段指出书结合地质、历史、经济和数据来解释城市发展。引入作者论文的是后半部分，B 的 throughout 范围太大。"],
      [67,"At first glance, ","it is not obvious why slum clearance would be limiting",", while more expensive foundations would not.","B。书评人质疑 Barr 为何视清理贫民区为限制，却不把更昂贵的地基视为限制；这是指出分析里的疑点。"],
      [68,"While less technical than the research paper on which the chapter is based, it is probably ","more technical than would be preferred by a general audience",".","C。与原论文比没那么技术化，但对普通读者仍偏专业。two comparisons 不能混读；没有说材料过时。"],
      [68,"Chapter eight contains lengthy discussions of urban economic theory that ","may serve as a distraction"," to readers primarily interested in New York.","D。城市经济学理论会让主要想了解纽约的读者分心，却适合经济学本科生；因此部分内容只对某些人有吸引力。"],
      [68,"","The data work that went into these estimations"," is particularly impressive.","C。书评用 particularly impressive 直接评价地价估算背后的数据研究。年代范围与所提因果问题是内容，并非被点名为最令人印象深刻。"],
      [67,"Barr begins chapter one by taking the reader on a ‘helicopter time-machine’ ride – ","giving a fascinating account"," of how the New York landscape in 1609 might have looked from the sky.","书评将 1609 年空中所见称为 fascinating，与 lacks interest 相反，判 NO。might have looked 仅表示是历史复原。"],
      [67,"Both chapters are informative and well researched and ","set the stage for the economic analysis"," that comes later in the book.","两章铺垫之后的经济分析，和 prepare the reader for material yet to come 一致，判 YES。"],
      [68,"Barr identifies four primary immigrant enclaves and analyzes their locations in terms of the ","amenities available in the area",".","文中说 Barr 用设施分布分析移民聚居地选择，没说所缺设施是最大问题，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [68,"Most of these enclaves were located on the least valuable land, ","between the industries located on the waterfront"," and the wealthy neighborhoods bordering Central Park.","多数移民社区在滨水工业与中央公园富裕社区之间的低价土地，不等于集中在港口周围。题干偷换地点，判 NO。"],
      [68,"… myth’, the assumption that the absence of bedrock close to the surface between Downtown and Midtown New York is the reason for skyscrapers not being built ","between the two urban centers",".","H。讨论的缺楼区域是 Downtown 与 Midtown 之间，属于 specific areas；不是讨论摩天楼普遍缺失。"],
      [68,"Rather, Barr argues that while deeper bedrock does increase foundation costs, these costs were ","neither prohibitively high"," nor were they large compared to the overall cost of building a skyscraper.","D。深岩床使地基变贵，但未贵到足以阻止开发；因此不能称作 excessive expense。"],
      [68,"Rather, Barr argues that while deeper bedrock does increase foundation costs, these costs were neither prohibitively high nor were they large compared to ","the overall cost of building a skyscraper",".","I。比较基准是造整栋楼的总成本，overall cost 对应 total expenditure；并非只比两处地基价格。"],
      [68,"He describes the use of caissons, which enable workers to ","dig down for considerable distances",", often below the water table, until they reach bedrock.","B。沉箱让工人向下挖很深，有时穿到地下水位以下。题目问它让什么工作成为可能，选 deep excavations。"],
      [68,"Barr’s thorough technological history discusses not only how caissons work, but also ","the dangers involved",".","F。Barr 讲沉箱如何工作，同时讨论施工危险。dangers involved 对应 associated risks。"]
    ],
    [
      [81,"Madagascar’s ","forests are being converted to agricultural land"," at a rate of one percent every year.","破坏森林的直接动作是农民清林扩种，昆虫攻击的是水稻等庄稼。题干把昆虫攻击的对象换成森林，判 FALSE。"],
      [81,"In fact, ","some of the island’s insectivorous bats are currently thriving"," and this has important implications for farmers and conservationists alike.","开头先交代总体生境损失，再说部分食虫蝙蝠正繁盛；下文还有它们利用改造后的稻田捕食的例子。题干断言它们已被严重打击，判 FALSE。"],
      [81,"More specifically, ","he’s interested in how bats are responding to human activity"," and deforestation in particular.","交代 Rocha 的研究兴趣和马达加斯加案例，没列他是否在世界其他地方做过研究。美国和加泰罗尼亚的已有成果也未归于 Rocha，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [81,"Co-leading an international team of scientists, Rocha found that several species of indigenous bats are ","taking advantage of habitat modification"," to hunt insects swarming above the country’s rice fields.","当地蝙蝠利用改造后的稻田捕食有害昆虫，给农民提供免费害虫防治。habitat modification 与 useful to farmers 两部分都有证据。"],
      [81,"","They include the Malagasy mouse-eared bat",", Major’s long-fingered bat, the Malagasy white-bellied free-tailed bat and Peters’ wrinkle-lipped bat.","鼠耳蝠是列出的几个本地物种之一，原文不比较它们的数量。先被列举不等于最常见，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [81,"‘We found that six species of bat are preying on rice pests, ","including the paddy swarming caterpillar and grass webworm",".","Rocha 将两种昆虫直接列为六种蝙蝠所猎食的稻田害虫，吻合题干的 may feed on，判 TRUE。"],
      [82,"They next used DNA barcoding techniques to ","analyse droppings collected from bats"," at the different sites.","超声录音用于定位捕食地点，下一步用 DNA 条形码分析粪便。表格问后者的样本，填 droppings，不能写 feeding buzzes。"],
      [82,"… benefits most from the bats, the scientists also found indications that the bats were consuming pests of other crops, including the black twig borer (","which infests coffee plants","), the sugarcane cicada, the macadamia nut-borer, and the sober tabby (a pest of citrus fruits).","原文按作物列害虫，black twig borer 危害咖啡树。表格并列的是作物品类，因此填 coffee 而非害虫名称。"],
      [82,"While the animal is often associated with spreading disease, Rocha and his team found evidence that Malagasy bats ","feed not just on crop pests but also on mosquitoes"," – carriers of malaria, Rift Valley fever virus and elephantiasis – as well as blackflies, which spread river blindness.","原文说还吃蚊子以及 blackflies，两者都是疾病传播媒介。题干已给 blackflies，填并列的 mosquitoes。"],
      [82,"When food is scarce, bats become ","a crucial source of protein"," for local people.","食物短缺时，有人猎食蝙蝠补充蛋白质。food rich in 对应 source of，按词数填 protein。"],
      [82,"And as well as roosting in trees, the bats sometimes roost in buildings, but are not welcomed there because ","they make them unclean",".","此处 they 指蝙蝠，them 指它们栖息的建筑。题目 become 后需要状态词 unclean，roost 表示栖息行为。"],
      [82,"At the same time, however, they are associated with sacred caves and the ancestors, so they can be viewed as beings between worlds, which makes them ","very significant in the culture of the people",".","和神圣洞穴、祖先相联系解释了蝙蝠在当地文化中的地位。important role 对应 very significant，填 culture。"],
      [82,"Rocha says, ‘With the right help, we hope that farmers can promote this mutually beneficial relationship ","by installing bat houses",".’","Rocha 希望农民安装人工蝙蝠屋，让它们有地方栖息。题干已经给 special，空格只填 houses。"],
      [86,"One way to look at whether education causes economic growth is to ‘","hold wealth constant","’.","E 段解释选择财富水平相同的人跟踪，以免财富差异掩盖教育与创新的关系。题干 focus on consistent income 指这个控制条件。"],
      [85,"It includes ","court records, guild ledgers, parish registers",", village censuses, tax lists and – the most recent addition – 9,000 handwritten inventories listing over a million personal possessions belonging to ordinary …","A 段开头列法院记录、行会账簿、教区登记、普查、税表及清单等资料来源。C 段列具体财物，两者范围不同。"],
      [86,"When ","Juliana continued taking jobs"," reserved for male guild members, she was summoned before the guild court and told to pay a fine equivalent to one third of a servant’s annual wage.","D 段的 Juliana 收到行会训诫后仍接只给男性成员的活，最后被传唤罚款。关键是 continued，表明她不服从。"],
      [86,"‘German-speaking central Europe is ","an excellent laboratory for testing"," theories of economic growth,’ she explains.","F 段把德语区中欧称为检验经济增长理论的理想场所：识字率和藏书高，地区依然贫穷。excellent laboratory 是比喻。"],
      [85,"","From badger skins to Bibles",", sewing machines to scarlet bodices – the villagers’ entire worldly goods are included.","C 段列獾皮、圣经、缝纫机和衣服等清单中的物品。A 段只说明此类清单进入数据库，没给这组例子。"],
      [86,"‘","We can follow the same people"," – and their descendants – across 300 years of educational and economic change,’ she says.","原文可跟踪同一些人及其后代跨越 300 年。as well as 对应 and，填复数 descendants。"],
      [86,"Stories like that of the 24-year-olds Ana Regina and Magdalena Riethmüllerin, who were chastised in 1707 for reading books in church ","instead of listening to the sermon",".","两位女士在教堂看书，原本应当听布道。paying attention to 对应 listening to，填 sermon。"],
      [86,"When Juliana continued taking jobs reserved for male guild members, she was summoned before the guild court and ","told to pay a fine"," equivalent to one third of a servant’s annual wage.","Juliana 后来被处以相当于仆人年薪三分之一的罚款。题干问处罚种类，不问金额。"],
      [86,"The dominance of guilds not only prevented people from using their skills, but also ","held back even the simplest industrial innovation",".","行会阻止别人使用技能，也延缓最基本的工业创新。prevent 对应 held back，填 innovation。"],
      [85,"During this period, ","Germany and Scandinavia had excellent literacy rates",", but their economies grew slowly and they industrialised late.","B。1600–1900 年德国与北欧识字率很好，却工业化晚。英格兰恰好是识字率平平却先工业化。B、E 顺序不限。"],
      [85,"‘Modern cross-country analyses have also struggled to find evidence that education causes economic growth, even though there is plenty of evidence that ","growth increases education",",’ she adds.","E。Ogilvie 说不少证据支持经济增长提高教育水平；反向的教育促增长证据难找。C 把方向倒置。"],
      [86,"In villages throughout the region, ","guilds blocked labour migration"," and resisted changes that might reduce their influence.","B。blocked labour migration 对应阻挡劳工为工作迁入或迁出。段落关注行会限制，不涉及技能培训。B、D 顺序不限。"],
      [86,"It was also the case that local guilds and merchant associations were extremely powerful and legislated against ","anything that undermined their monopolies",".","D。行会立规则反对削弱垄断的活动，也抵制会降低影响力的变化。trade control 对应 monopolies。"],
      [89,"But ","displays of the feat go back centuries",".","D 段举佛罗伦萨十三世纪对局和 Najdorf 1947 年盲下 45 局。earlier examples 是历史实例，C 段则是 Gareyev 自己学棋史。"],
      [89,"Not only ","must the positions of each piece on every board be memorised",", they must be recalled faithfully when needed, updated with each player’s moves, and then reliably stored again, so the brain can move on to the next board.","E 段说明如何记住每盘棋、调出局面、更新落子再存回；题目问盲下到底要做什么。"],
      [90,"‘We didn’t find ","anything other than playing chess"," that he seems to be supremely gifted at.’","F 段 Rissman 说标准记忆测试不出众，没发现他棋艺之外也如此出色。B 段只谈能同时下很多局。"],
      [89,"","In the hope of understanding how"," he and others like him can perform such mental feats, researchers at the University of California in Los Angeles (UCLA) called him in for tests.","B 段 UCLA 想弄懂他和类似棋手怎样完成多局盲下，先说明研究动机。F 段才给测试和扫描结果。"],
      [90,"‘The most important part of blindfold chess for me is that I have found the ","one thing that I can fully dedicate myself to",".","H 段 Gareyev 说最看重找到能全心投入的事，并不太担心胜率。priorities 问的是他的取舍，47 局等是比赛要求。"],
      [90,"But the ends of games are taxing too, ","as exhaustion sets in",".","E 段说对局末尾因疲劳而愈发费力，回忆棋位会变零碎。开局难记是因为招法平淡，两个阶段原因不同。"],
      [89,"While ","his challengers will play the games as normal",", Gareyev himself will be blindfolded.","对手正常下棋，Gareyev 才蒙眼。题干说 all participants，因此判 FALSE。"],
      [89,"He has a fondness for bright clothes and unusual hairstyles, and ","he gets his kicks from the adventure sport"," of BASE jumping.","A 段只说他喜欢 BASE jumping，没提参赛或夺冠纪录。兴趣不能推出赢过比赛，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [89,"In the hope of understanding how he and others like him can perform such mental feats, ","researchers at the University of California"," in Los Angeles (UCLA) called him in for tests.","B、F 段交代 UCLA 做研究并有首批结果，没有把它和其他大学的时间比较。their first results 不等于全球最早，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [89,"‘The ability to play a game of chess with your eyes closed is ","not a far reach for most accomplished players",",’ said Jesse Rissman, who runs a memory lab at UCLA.","Rissman 说大多数高水平棋手盲下一局并不难；罕见的是同时进行的局数。题干只说盲下能力，所以 TRUE。"],
      [90,"F The scientists first had Gareyev ","perform some standard memory tests",".","第一阶段测他在脑中记数字、图片、词语的能力。for example 后数字回忆只是其中一种题，空格填总能力 memory。"],
      [90,"One classic test measures ","how many numbers a person can repeat",", both forwards and backwards, soon after hearing them.","both forwards and backwards 对应 in order and in reverse order。题干问他复述什么，填复数 numbers。"],
      [90,"Though the results are tentative and as yet unpublished, the scans found much ","greater than average communication"," between parts of Gareyev’s brain that make up what is called the frontoparietal control network.","扫描看到负责注意力的额顶控制网络内部沟通高于平均。unusual amount 对应 greater than average，填 communication。"],
      [90,"Initial results suggest that ","the areas of his brain that process visual images"," – such as chess boards – may have stronger links to other brain regions, and so be more powerful than normal.","G 段说处理棋盘等视觉图像的脑区可能连接更强。空格修饰 input，所以填形容词 visual，不填 images。"]
    ]
  ],
  18: [
    [
      [18,"From identical vertical tubes nearby ","burst row upon row of lettuces","; near those are aromatic herbs, such as basil, sage and peppermint.","草莓和生菜都长在同类直立塑料管里，香草在旁边。后面樱桃番茄用的是水平托盘，题干限定 vertical tubes，填 lettuces。"],
      [18,"When the remaining two thirds of the vast open area are in production, 20 staff will ","harvest up to 1,000 kg"," of perhaps 35 different varieties of fruit and vegetables, every day.","remaining two thirds 投产以后，20 人每天最多收获 1,000 kg。up to 对应 as much as，填重量含单位。3,000 是已采的生菜株数。"],
      [18,"But if enough unused space can be developed like this, there's no reason why you shouldn't eventually target maybe ","between 5% and 10% of consumption",".","Hardy 说若能开发足够空间，可能达到消费量的 5%–10%。as much as 10% 是上限，空格填 consumption 或 food consumption。"],
      [18,"'First, I don't much like the fact that most of the fruit and vegetables we eat have been ","treated with something like 17 different pesticides",", or that the intensive farming techniques that produced them are such huge generators of greenhouse gases.","这里批评传统集约农产用了约 17 种杀虫剂或农药，正是 a wide range of 的证据。温室气体是生产的另一项问题。"],
      [19,"… travelled an average of 2,000 refrigerated kilometres to my plate, that their quality is so poor, because the varieties are selected for their capacity ","to withstand such substantial journeys",", or that 80% of the price I pay goes to wholesalers and transport companies, not the producers.","withstand 对应 survive，品种为经得住远距离冷链运输而选。空格 long 后填 journeys；quality poor 是这种选种带来的结果。"],
      [19,"… varieties are selected for their capacity to withstand such substantial journeys, or that 80% of the price I pay goes to wholesalers and transport companies, ","not the producers",".","售价约八成给批发与运输公司，生产者拿到的份额很小。表格问谁 receive very little，反向抓 not the producers。"],
      [19,"'You can ","select crop varieties for their flavour",", not their resistance to the transport and storage chain, and you can pick them when they're really at their best, and not before.","少运输让选种能优先考虑风味，而非耐运输耐储存。because of 对应 for，空格填 flavour 或 flavor。"],
      [19,"Strawberries are being grown in disused shipping containers, ","mushrooms in underground carparks",".","开头有屋顶种植，后文有地下停车场种蘑菇，分别验证 above 和 below ground。题目说 can，不要求同一家农场同时在两处种。"],
      [19,"The ","equipment weighs little",", can be installed on almost any flat surface and is cheap to buy: roughly €100 to €150 per square metre.","原文给出设备轻、可安装、便宜且省电，未说明其中任何设备可手工制作。安装方便不能推出 made by hand，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [19,"It is cheap to run, too, consuming ","a tiny fraction of the electricity"," used by some techniques.","a tiny fraction of 表示只有部分其他技术用电量的一小部分，方向与题干 relies more 相反，判 FALSE。"],
      [19,"Produce grown this way typically sells at prices that, while generally higher than those of classic intensive agriculture, are ","lower than soil-based organic growers",".","同一种城市农产品，比传统集约种植贵，但比土壤有机种植便宜。题干指定比较对象是后者，判 TRUE。"],
      [19,"There are limits to what farmers can grow this way, of course, and ","much of the produce is suited to the summer months",".","原文给出夏季适宜和适种作物限制，直接否定大部分产品随时全年都能种的说法。"],
      [19,"And ","beans tend to take up a lot of space"," for not much return.","只交代豆类占地大、收益小。没有把豆类的生长时间跟其他蔬菜比较，不能因空间成本推断花时更长，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [22,"These trees have lower economic value for traditional timber markets, compete for growth with higher-value trees, shade out desirable regeneration and ","decrease the health of a stand","* leaving it more vulnerable to poor weather and disease.","B 段说只砍优质林木的 high-grading 会留下低质树，竞争资源、遮挡幼苗并降低林分健康。这些是只顾经济价值的坏结果。"],
      [22,"A ","A tree's 'value' depends on"," several factors including its species, size, form, condition, quality, function, and accessibility, and depends on the management goals for a given forest.","A 段列树种、尺寸、形状、状态、功能和可达性，并说明管理目标不同也改变评估。题目问估值要素，非哪种木最赚钱。"],
      [22,"Wood can also be gasified for electrical generation and can even be made into ","liquid fuels like ethanol"," and gasoline for lorries and cars.","C 段说明低用途木能制成汽车卡车用乙醇或汽油，正是木材间接驱动车辆。锅炉供热、发电是同段的其他用途。"],
      [23,"With the many pests and pathogens visiting forests including ","hemlock wooly adelgid",", Asian longhorned beetle, emerald ash borer, and gypsy moth, to name just a few, it is important to remember that those working in the forests can help …","E 段介绍抢救性采伐时列击树害虫，例如 adelgid 和各类甲虫、蛾。末段的啄木鸟和蝙蝠是害虫天敌。"],
      [22,"Some people even ","call these 'junk trees","', and they are abundant in Pennsylvania.","B 段直接给出 low-use wood 这些树另被称作 junk trees。题目找别称，别把导致它们留下的 high-grading 当成名称。"],
      [23,"These types of cut ","reduce the number of sick trees"," and seek to manage the future spread of a pest problem.","B 对应 Salvage Cut。E 段说该法减少病树、限制虫害扩散，并保留健康树。TSI Cut 重点是给好树腾出空间。"],
      [23,"It can also be used to develop a two-tier forest so that there are two harvests and ","the money that comes in is spread out"," over a decade or more.","C 对应 Shelterwood Cut。F 段说两期采收可让收入分散到十年甚至更久，吻合 across a number of years。"],
      [23,"It leaves a young forest where all trees are ","at a similar point in their growth",".","C。庇护伐待幼苗建立后移除成熟树，留下发育阶段相近的幼树。close in age 换写了 similar point in growth。"],
      [23,"G Thinnings and dense and ","dead wood removal for fire prevention"," also center on the production of low-use wood.","去除部分枯死木是做防火处理，for fire prevention 对应 avoid the possibility of fire。后文提醒并非所有低用途木都要移走。"],
      [23,"The tops of trees that have been cut down should be left on the site so that ","their nutrients cycle back into the soil",".","树冠残留原地，让养分回到土壤。题干问的是从树梢回到土壤的东西，填 nutrients，不填 tree tops。"],
      [23,"In addition, ","trees with many cavities"," are extremely important habitats for insect predators like woodpeckers, bats and small mammals.","树洞为啄木鸟、蝙蝠等提供栖所。这些动物控制害虫，说明为什么要保留这样的树，空格填复数 cavities。"],
      [23,"For example, ","many species like hawthorn provide food"," for wildlife.","原文举 hawthorn 说明小树也能供食，并非都低用途。such as 提示找具体例子，填 hawthorn。"],
      [23,"Finally, ","rare species of trees in a forest should also stay behind"," as they add to its structural diversity.","原文让稀有树种留下，以增加结构多样性。trees that are 后缺形容词 rare。"],
      [27,"That means companies, governments and other players in space are ","collaborating in new ways to avoid a shared threat",".","C 段直接描述企业、政府等为规避共同威胁展开协作，并以国际组织指南为例。avoid a shared threat 对应 minimise risk。"],
      [28,"Jah describes himself as a space environmentalist: 'I want to make space a place that is ","safe to operate, that is free and useful"," for generations to come.'","F 段末尾 Jah 说想让太空安全、开放、可供后代使用。这是他个人目标的直接引语，不是 D 段的技术方法。"],
      [27,"Ten years ago, a US commercial Iridium satellite ","smashed into an inactive Russian communications satellite"," called Cosmos-2251 creating thousands of new pieces of space shrapnel that now threaten other satellites in low Earth orbit — the zone stretching up to …","A 段描述 Iridium 与 Cosmos-2251 相撞，产生数千块碎片。B 段主要设想将来连锁撞击，不是已经发生的事故。"],
      [28,"","Air-traffic controllers know the location"," of the planes down to one metre in accuracy.","E 段对比机场飞机能定位至米级，太空对象却没全登记、跟踪也不一致。题目要求与地面或航空运输系统的类比。"],
      [27,"Others are ","developing taxonomies of space debris"," — working on measuring properties such as the shape and size of an object, so that satellite operators know how much to worry about what's coming their way.","B 段说研究者尝试量碎片的形状和大小来分类。taxonomies 就是分类体系，区别于精确知道每块碎片的轨道。"],
      [27,"International groups such as the Inter-Agency Space Debris Coordination Committee have ","developed guidelines on space sustainability",".","题干 how ... can be achieved 对应关于如何维持空间可用性的 guidelines。space 在空后已给，填 sustainability。"],
      [27,"Those include inactivating satellites at the end of their useful life by venting pressurised materials or ","leftover fuel"," that might lead to explosions.","unused 对应 leftover，题干已给另一项 pressurised material。要排出的是剩余 fuel，不是卫星整机。"],
      [27,"Those include inactivating satellites at the end of their useful life by venting pressurised materials or leftover fuel ","that might lead to explosions",".","排掉余燃料或加压材料是因为它们可能爆炸。could cause 对应 might lead to，填复数 explosions。"],
      [28,"'What happens to those that fail or ","go bankrupt","?'","Krag 质疑运营商破产后是否愿花钱把卫星移除。become 对应 go，后接形容词 bankrupt；题干不问他们为什么破产。"],
      [28,"'","If you knew precisely where everything was",", you would almost never have a problem,' says Marlon Sorge, a space-debris specialist at the Aerospace Corporation in El Segundo, California.","C 是 Sorge。他说若精确知道所有对象的位置，几乎不会有问题，也能少做无谓机动。precisely 对应 exact location。"],
      [28,"Jah describes himself as a space environmentalist: 'I want to make space a place that is safe to operate, that is free and useful ","for generations to come",".'","D 是 Jah。他希望太空安全、免费可用并传给后代，available to everyone 对应 free，可保留到 future 对应 generations to come。"],
      [28,"But so far, ","only about half of all missions"," have abided by this 25-year goal, says Holger Krag, head of the European Space Agency's space-debris office in Darmstadt, Germany.","B 是 Krag。约一半任务遵守 25 年内烧毁或解体的目标，说明不少任务没遵照。这里是国际建议，不是 Jah 的数据库。"],
      [28,"When Jah enters that number, the database draws two purple lines: the US and Russian sources contain ","two completely different orbits"," for the same object.","D 是 Jah。他的数据库把同一俄罗斯火箭体画成两条轨道，因为美俄目录不同。two orbits 对应 conflicting information。"],
      [27,"'If we go on like this, we will reach ","a point of no return",",' says Carolin Frueh, an astrodynamical researcher at Purdue University in West Lafayette, Indiana.","A 是 Frueh。她警告继续相撞会造成碎片连锁反应、使近地空间无法使用。no return 对应无法挽回。"]
    ],
    [
      [41,"First, Neolithic* Britons used primitive tools, which may have been ","fashioned out of deer antlers",", to dig a massive circular ditch and bank, or henge.","原文是挖沟渠的原始工具可能由鹿角制成。made from 对应 fashioned out of，填 antlers 或 deer antlers，保留 may have 的不确定性。"],
      [41,"Deep pits dating back to that era and located within the circle may have once ","held a ring of timber posts",", according to some scholars.","圆圈里的深坑可能支撑一圈木柱。题目把坑作主语换成木柱 placed/arranged，填 posts 或 timber posts。"],
      [41,"According to one long-standing theory among archaeologists, Stonehenge's builders fashioned ","sledges and rollers out of tree trunks"," to lug the bluestones from the Preseli Hills.","考古学旧说用树干制雪橇和滚轴，to make 对应 fashioned out of。筏子是沿海和河道运输的后续工具。"],
      [41,"More recent archaeological hypotheses have them transporting the bluestones with supersized wicker baskets on a combination of ball bearings and long grooved planks, ","hauled by oxen",".","新假说是牛拖动装石的巨篮，另有滚珠、带槽木板配合。pulled 对应 hauled，空格问动力来源 oxen。"],
      [41,"Challenging the classic image of industrious builders pushing, carting, rolling or hauling giant stones from faraway Wales, some scientists have suggested that ","it was glaciers, not humans",", that carried the bluestones to Salisbury Plain.","地质学家的不同说法是冰川把石头从威尔士搬来。glaciers 对应 geological theory，人力属于对比的另一说。"],
      [42,"In the 17th century, archaeologist John Aubrey made the claim that Stonehenge ","was the work of druids",", who had important religious, judicial and political roles in Celtic\" society.","Aubrey 在十七世纪提出由凯尔特祭司建造。题干已有 Celtic，填 druids。这是旧假说，后文并未证实。"],
      [42,"While there is consensus among the majority of modern scholars that Stonehenge once served ","the function of burial ground",", they have yet to determine what other purposes it had.","现代学者多数同意至少曾作墓地。题干已给 site，写 burial，与 burial ground 同义。其他用途仍不明确。"],
      [42,"In the 1960s, the astronomer Gerald Hawkins suggested that the cluster of megalithic stones ","operated as a form of calendar",", with different points corresponding to astrological phenomena such as solstices, equinoxes and eclipses occurring at different times of the year.","Hawkins 在 1960 年代认为石位对应一年中分至、日月食等现象。worked as a kind of 换写 operated as a form of。"],
      [42,"At this point, sandstone slabs — known as 'sarsens' — were arranged ","into an outer crescent or ring","; some were assembled into the iconic three-pieced structures called trilithons that stand tall in the centre of Stonehenge.","第三阶段砂岩一部分在外围，一部分组成居中的 trilithons。both outer and middle 两处在同段分别有证据，所以 TRUE。"],
      [42,"Radiocarbon dating has revealed that work continued at Stonehenge until roughly 1600 BCE, with the bluestones in particular ","being repositioned multiple times",".","碳测年显示工程持续至约 1600 BCE，并且青石多次重新摆位。same spot 与 repositioned multiple times 直接矛盾，判 FALSE。"],
      [42,"However, in the mid-20th century, radiocarbon dating demonstrated that Stonehenge stood ","more than 1 ,000 years before the Celts"," inhabited the region.","Aubrey 称建造者是凯尔特德鲁伊，二十世纪测年却显示遗址早于凯尔特人到来一千多年。新证据推翻他的说法，判 FALSE。"],
      [42,"","Bones, tools and other artefacts"," found on the site seem to support this hypothesis.","器物与遗骸看起来支持几个不同部落分期施工。题干 objects ... seem to indicate 保留了原文的推测程度。"],
      [42,"While his theory has received a considerable amount of attention over the decades, ","critics maintain that Stonehenge's builders"," probably lacked the knowledge necessary to predict such events or that England's dense cloud cover would have obscured their view of the skies.","文章交代批评内容，包括建造者知识是否足够、云层是否遮挡天空，却没说批评者主要做天文学，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [45,"But many experts believe ","this restriction is very temporary",".","C。首段用会下棋的 AI 引出眼下只做专门任务，专家认为这种限制短暂，可能发展到通用水平。不是在争论下棋技术。"],
      [45,"","Machines will be free of many of the physical constraints"," on human intelligence.","A。作者用大脑化学处理慢、尺寸受生理条件限制解答机器为何能超越人。说的是差异的后果，不是共性。"],
      [45,"But the more powerful Al becomes, the more important it will be to ","specify its goals with great care",".","B。Midas 想让所触物变金，却没料到早餐也变金。例子说明目标写得不周全会产生不想要的结果，不在于赚钱。"],
      [45,"If superintelligent machines ","don't do a lot better than us",", we'll be in deep trouble.","D。人并非一直善待彼此，照搬人的行为会放大我们的缺点，所以机器得比人更友善。第四段强调这个门槛。"],
      [46,"For safety's sake, then, we want the machines to be ","ethically as well as cognitively superhuman",".","C。作者说机器在认知、找伦理上策方面可能超过人类。段落的重点是能在哪些方面胜过，并非人们抵制。"],
      [46,"This won't be easy, given that ","we are tribal creatures and conflicted"," about the ideals ourselves.","D。如何给 AI 指明伦理目标，本来就难，因为人偏袒自己群体，对理想也有分歧。障碍是人的局限，而不是缺程序员。"],
      [46,"We might ","lose our freedom to discriminate in favour of our own communities",", for example.","作者说道德机器可能限制偏袒自己社群的自由，正对应 may prevent us from promoting their interests。may 表示可能，判 YES。"],
      [46,"","They might be so good at doing it"," that we won't notice them; but few of us are likely to welcome such a future.","原文讨论限制可能高效得不让人察觉，但不提需要多少台。效果和数量是不同信息，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [46,"They might be so good at doing it that we won't notice them; but ","few of us are likely to welcome"," such a future.","作者预计很少人欢迎被机器限制，和 many people are comfortable 正相反。该段关于禁童工的例子不能证明喜欢 AI 限制。"],
      [46,"It is not yet clear whether this is possible, but if it is, ","it will require a cooperative spirit",", and a willingness to set aside self-interest.","让机器替我们得当行事，作者称需要合作并搁置个人私利。cooperative spirit 对应 work together，判 YES。"],
      [46,"Al already has some input into how ","resources are used"," in our National Health Service (NHS) here in the I-JK, for example.","C。NHS 已让 AI 参与安排资源用到哪里。used and allocated 都涉及分配，填 available resources；效率是扩大参与后的好处。"],
      [46,"However, we'd be depriving some humans (e.g. ","senior doctors",") of the control they presently enjoy.","A。文中用资深医生举例，说明部分医务人员会失去现有控制权。空格是人，不能填后面的权力。"],
      [46,"However, we'd be depriving some humans (e.g. senior doctors) of ","the control they presently enjoy",".","E。医生目前拥有的 control 是 professional authority。题干说失去 current level，不是说病患数量减少。"],
      [50,"","Five hundred years have passed since Leonardo died"," in his home at Chåteau du Clos Lucé, outside Tours, France.","五百年指达·芬奇去世至今，另说他现在常被称天才。文中没有这种称呼第一次出现的时间，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [50,"Today, the world is on the cusp of a climate crisis, which is ","predicted to cause widespread displacement",", extinctions and death, if left unaddressed.","瘟疫死亡约两亿，气候危机只预测流离失所、灭绝和死亡，无两者死亡人数对比，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [50,"","Then, as now",", radical solutions were called for to revolutionise the way people lived and safeguard humanity against catastrophe.","昔日瘟疫与今天气候危机都需要改变生活方式的激进办法，then, as now 直接作了类比，支持题干。"],
      [50,"Following a typical Renaissance trend, he began to work on an 'ideal city' project, which due to its excessive costs ","would remain unfulfilled",".","1486 年左右开始设计，但费用太高，项目没有实现。设计起始时间不能当成建成时间，判 FALSE。"],
      [50,"Yet given that ","unsustainable urban models are a key cause"," of global climate change today, it's only natural to wonder how Leonardo might have changed the shape of modern cities.","不可持续的城市模式是气候变化的主要成因之一。poor town planning 对应 unsustainable urban models，major contributor 对应 key cause。"],
      [50,"… had been largely missing in Western thought until the moment when prominent Renaissance men pushed forward large-scale urban projects in Italy, such as ","the reconfiguration of the town of Pienza"," and the expansion of the city of Ferrara.","文中列 Pienza 改造与 Ferrara 扩张作当时项目，只谈对达·芬奇的启发，没说本地居民反抗或支持，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [50,"It is not easy to identify a coordinated vision of Leonardo's ideal city because of ","his disordered way of working"," with notes and sketches.","笔记和草图杂乱，难以从中拼出整体设计。与 neat, organised 直接相反，判 FALSE。"],
      [50,"He designed the city for the ","easy transport of goods"," and clean urban spaces, and he wanted a comfortable and spacious city, with well-ordered streets and architecture.","原文设计让货物好运输、空间更清洁；题干 for trade 改述 of goods，空格填 transport。"],
      [51,"Leonardo wanted the city to be built on several levels, linked with ","vertical outdoor staircases",".","多个楼层由外部楼梯连接，这种设计后来在部分高楼出现。outside/exterior 对应 outdoor，填复数 staircases。"],
      [51,"But the true originality of Leonardo's vision was its ","fusion of architecture and engineering",".","输水设施和人工运河表明他把工程与建筑结合，空格问另一领域，填 engineering。hydraulic 修饰一个类别而非学科名。"],
      [51,"Leonardo also thought that the width of the streets ought to match the average height of the adjacent houses: ","a rule still followed"," in many contemporary cities across Italy, to allow access to sun and reduce the risk of damage from earthquakes.","道路宽度对应周边房屋平均高度，既能进光又可减轻地震风险。意大利不少现代城市仍遵循它，this 后填 rule。"],
      [51,"Although ","some of these features existed in Roman cities",", before Leonardo's drawings there had never been a multi-level, compact modern city which was thoroughly technically conceived.","某些元素在古罗马城市已存在，但其技术化多层整合是新的。题干 times 前填 Roman。"],
      [51,"… infrastructures located in the lower levels and wide and well-ventilated boulevards and walkways above for residents is an idea that can be found in Georges-Eugéne ","Haussmann 's renovation of Paris"," under Emperor Napoleon III between 1853 and 1870.","1853–1870 年 Haussmann 改造巴黎，较低层安排服务设施、较高层为居民提供通道。例子问城市，填 Paris。"],
      [51,"Many scholars think that the compact city, ","built upwards instead of outwards",", integrated with nature (especially water systems), with effcient transport infrastructure, could help modern cities become more efficient and sustainable.","紧凑城市向上建而非向外铺开。题干 no longer seems to be the best 对应被放弃的 outwards，别填被建议的 upwards。"]
    ],
    [
      [64,"Fly ash, ","a byproduct of coal-burning power plants",", can be incorporated into concrete mixes to make up as much as 15 to 30% of the cement, without harming the strength or durability of the resulting mix.","G 段分别交代粉煤灰来自燃煤发电，矿渣来自冶炼铁矿。题干找可掺入混凝土的原料如何产生，强调工业来源。"],
      [63,"","Vancouver, Vienna and Brumunddal"," in Norway are all home to constructed tall, wooden buildings.","D 段列 Vancouver、Vienna 和挪威 Brumunddal 已有木质高楼。F 段的芬兰、亚洲主要说明供应和需求变化。"],
      [63,"C Not only are the ingredients of concrete relatively cheap and ","found in abundance in most places"," around the globe, the stuff itself has marvellous properties: Portland cement, the vital component of concrete, is mouldable and pourable, but quickly sets hard.","C 段说混凝土原料便宜且全球大多数地方供应充足。widely available 对应 found in abundance，不只是使用量大。"],
      [64,"But even treated wood has its limitations and only when ","a wider range of construction projects"," has been proven in practice will it be possible to see wood as a real alternative to concrete in constructing tall buildings.","F 段最后说木材要在更多类型工程中证明确实可行，才能成为高楼用混凝土的替代。当前需求升高不等于已验证。"],
      [63,"Making buildings from wood may seem like a rather medieval idea, but climate change is ","driving architects to turn to treated timber"," as a possible resource.","气候变化让建筑师转向处理木材。题目问受环境问题推动的是谁，填 architects；treated timber 是选用的材料。"],
      [64,"","Wood expands as it absorbs moisture"," from the air and is susceptible to pests, not to mention fire.","increases in size 对应 expands，enters wood 对应 absorbs。来自空气的东西是 moisture，虫害和火灾是并列困难。"],
      [64,"An adhesive is used to ","stick layers of solid-sawn timber together",", crosswise, to form building blocks.","glued 对应 stick。交叉粘合的是实锯木材的多层，空格填复数 layers；adhesive 是胶本身。"],
      [64,"Construction experts say that wooden buildings can be ","constructed at a greater speed"," than ones of concrete and steel and the process, it seems, is quieter.","题干 with which they can be constructed 问施工速度。后面说过程也更安静，已由 how much noise 表达。"],
      [64,"If they are ","transported over long distances",", using fossil fuels, the use of alternative materials might not make sense from an overall carbon reduction perspective.","C 是 Surgenor。废料替代水泥虽可降碳，但远运耗化石燃料，可能冲掉效益。她要求看全生命周期。"],
      [63,"","Making anything with similar properties"," is going to be very difficult.'","A 是 Cheeseman。他说混凝土既易塑形又快硬，还可用钢强化，找到同等性能的替代很难。不是在评价某家公司。"],
      [64,"… cross-laminated timber, and its vice-president Markus Mannström reports that the company is seeing increasing demand globally for building in wood, with ","climate change concerns the key driver",".","B 是 Mannström。他把木建筑需求在全球上升主要归因于气候担忧，正对应 worries led to increased interest。"],
      [64,"At present, these alternatives are ","rarely as cost-effective as conventional cement",", and they face raw-material shortages and resistance from customers.","D 是 Preston 和 Lehne。新水泥往往不如普通水泥划算，还缺原料、客户抵触。题干问其中一个影响因素，expense 符合。"],
      [63,"But it is ","the scale on which it is used"," that makes it high carbon.","A 是 Cheeseman。他区分水泥与混凝土，认为混凝土被大量生产使用才让整体排放高。large quantities 对应 sheer scale。"],
      [68,"But these early cars ","inherited steam's weaknesses along with its strengths",".","iii。A 段介绍火车蒸汽技术移到汽车后，同时保留好处与手点火、慢升压、短续航等弱点。标题要覆盖两面。"],
      [68,"","A new technology called the Internal Combustion Engine"," soon appeared, which offered the ability to drive down the road just moments after starting up.","viii。B 段介绍内燃机能几乎立即开车，电启动解决手摇问题后蒸汽车逐渐退出。重点是更好的方案出现。"],
      [68,"Though the Doble boys' third prototype, nicknamed the Model B, still lacked the convenience of an internal combustion engine, ","it drew the attention of automobile trade magazines"," due to its numerous improvements over previous steam cars.","vi。C 段从早期原型写到受汽车杂志肯定的 Model B，并举安静、少烧焦气味、加速快三项。不是量产订单。"],
      [68,"By the following April, the General Engineering Company had ","received 5,390 deposits"," for Doble Detroits, which were scheduled for delivery in early 1918.","v。D 段先说 Model C 加钥匙点火等改良，末尾是 5,390 份订金。标题必须同时涵盖继续改良与带来订单。"],
      [69,"Those buyers who received the handful of completed cars ","complained that the vehicles were sluggish and erratic",", sometimes going in reverse when they should go forward.","vii。E 段转述等待交车的顾客失望，有人收到的车迟钝、不稳甚至方向反了。文段说的是到手结果。"],
      [69,"","After sitting overnight in freezing temperatures",", the car was pushed out into the road and left to sit for over an hour in the frosty morning air.","i。F 段先说 Model E 在低温中放了一夜，随后在严寒中点火路试。低温是测前条件，成绩是后续检验。"],
      [69,"Under the current pressure to improve automotive performance and reduce emissions, it is not unthinkable that ","the steam car may rise again",".","iv。G 段先回顾商业失败，但以现存车的耐用低排放与现代技术前景作结。标题要体现可能应对今日效率和排放要求。"],
      [68,"B But ","the glory days of steam cars were few",".","A。B 段说蒸汽车辉煌短暂，内燃机出现并加电启动后被取代。手摇困难早期主要说的是汽油车。"],
      [68,"Though it did not run well, the Doble brothers went on to build ","a second and third prototype"," in the following years.","C。首辆用旧车零件改装且表现欠佳，兄弟继续做第二、第三辆，Model B 才具竞争力。零件并非全自制。"],
      [68,"D The following year Abner Doble drove the Model B from Massachusetts to Detroit in order ","to seek investment in his automobile design",", which he used to open the General Engineering Company.","B。Abner 开 Model B 去 Detroit 寻投资，凭资金开公司，然后研发 Model C。旅行是融资手段，没有说迁移工厂是生产前提。"],
      [69,"As the new Doble steamer was further developed and tested, ","its maximum speed was pushed"," to over a hundred miles per hour, and it achieved about fifteen miles per gallon of kerosene with negligible emissions.","后续开发把 Model E 最高时速提高到逾 100 英里，同时排放小。空格问提高的指标，填 speed。"],
      [69,"By the time the company folded in 1931, ","fewer than fifty"," of the amazing Model E steam cars had been produced.","under 对应 fewer than，公司倒闭前产 Model E 不到 50 辆。价格约 $18,000 和倒闭年份都不是数量。"],
      [69,"Astonishingly, an unmodified Doble Model E runs clean enough to pass ","the emissions laws in California today",", and they are pretty strict.","原文说未经改造的 Model E 仍能达标，并说规则相当严格。空格在 emissions laws 前要形容词 strict。"],
      [72,"The teacher can ask the No Fear group to ","identify the key characters"," and maybe provide a tentative plot summary.","B。老师让需要支持者认人物和梳理情节、进阶者引文本、最强者探讨主题。场景示范如何应付不同学习需求。"],
      [72,"The practice is ","intuitively appealing to almost every stakeholder",".","A。原文说对几乎各方都有直观吸引力，对应 very broad appeal。该段介绍做法，没有说执行容易。"],
      [72,"","The brightest ones will never summit Mount Qomolangma",", and the stragglers won't enjoy the lovely stroll in the park they are perhaps more suited to.","C。登不到珠峰比喻最强学生无法达到可能达到的最高水平。作者此处在转述对混合班的批评，不是建议真去登山。"],
      [72,"The purpose of teaching is to ","provide and then gradually remove"," this 'scaffolding' until they are autonomous.","C。scaffolding 指学生尚不能独立完成任务时，老师、教材、例题、家长给的支撑，熟练后逐步撤去。ZPD 是差距，并不是支撑本身。"],
      [73,"Professor John Hattie, director of the Melboume Education Research Institute, notes that '","tracking has minimal effects on learning outcomes","'.","H。文献对分层带来更高成绩的支持很少，minimal effects 与 little indication 同义。空格考期待的总体效果 higher achievements。"],
      [73,"What is more, streaming appears to significantly — and negatively affect ","those students assigned to the lowest sets",".","D。受负面影响较明显的是分到低能力组的人，lowest sets 对应 bottom sets，并不说他们都被分错了。"],
      [73,"These students tend to have ","much higher representation of low socioeconomic class",".","F。低能力组更常见社会经济地位较低的学生，disadvantaged backgrounds 说的是家庭或社会背景。"],
      [73,"Less significant is ","the small benefit for those lucky clever students"," in the higher sets.","E。higher sets 里的较强学生只有小收益，对应 brightest pupils 与 minimal advantage。不是一般学生。"],
      [73,"Streaming students by diagnosed achievement ","automatically limits what the teacher feels"," the student is capable of.","B。分组诊断让教师对学生能达到什么水平的预期受限。混合班教师估计须更灵活，空格选 lower expectations。"],
      [72,"If we accept this model, it follows that ","streaming students with similar ZPDs"," would be an effcient and effective solution.","按该模型找相似最近发展区，作者指出逻辑上看似适合分层；题干说这个模型支持混合能力班，方向相反，判 NO。"],
      [73,"While teachers are traditionally the MKOs in classrooms, ","the value of knowledgeable student peers"," must not go unrecognised either.","作者自己主张同伴可成为更有知识者，但没有描述其他老师是否不确定该给学生这种角色，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [73,"There is also ","something exciting about passing on skills"," and knowledge that you yourself have just mastered a certain pride and zeal, a certain freshness to the interaction between 'teacher' and 'learner' that …","作者说传授刚掌握的技能会有新鲜感、骄傲和热情。rewarding 对应这些积极感受，判 YES。"],
      [73,"And today, more than ever, ","we need the many to flourish"," — not suffer at the expense of a few bright stars.","结尾强调让更多学生发展，不能为了少数尖子牺牲其他人。题干把尖子达标设为优先，判 NO。"],
      [73,"","We make it together",".","徒步例子展示互励、分担与合作，作者并未比较参加徒步前后课堂学习成绩。不能把合作实况当成测得的课堂效果，判 NOT GIVEN。"]
    ],
    [
      [87,"Other considerations include installing drainage paths, ","meeting health and safety requirements"," and perhaps allowing access for the public, as well as planning restrictions and disruption from regular activities in and around the buildings during installation.","D 段列维护技能、排水、健康安全、公众通行及规划限制等实施前须处理的事。题目要安装难点，不是列建成后的环境好处。"],
      [86,"","Toronto, Canada, has policies dating from the 1990s",", encouraging the development of urban farms on rooftops.","C 段说多伦多相关政策始于 1990 年代，符合 many years。旧金山虽同段提到，却由 only recently 标定。"],
      [87,"","The success stories need to be studied and replicated elsewhere",", to make green, blue, brown and food-producing roofs the norm in cities around the world.","E 段结尾说要研究成功案例并在别处复制，正是把现有成功屋顶当范本。前面的技术标准说明如何保证施工质量。"],
      [86,"B Ongoing research is showcasing how ","green roofs in cities can integrate with"," 'living walls': environmentally friendly walls which are partially or completely covered with greenery, including a growing medium, such as soil or water.","B 段举与覆绿墙面、地面排水和街道树木结合的例子。combination with other initiatives 对应 integrate with。"],
      [87,"To convince investors and developers that installing green roofs is worthwhile, ","economic arguments are still the most important",".","D 段说要说服投资人和开发商，经济理由仍最重要，并用避免洪害等带来的节省衡量自然价值。重点是财务论证。"],
      [86,"Among the benefits are ","saving on energy costs",", mitigating the risk of floods, making habitats for urban wildlife, tackling air pollution and even growing food.","题干 reducing how much money is spent on 对应 saving on ... costs。防洪与野生动物栖息地已经写出，补 energy。"],
      [86,"Among the benefits are saving on energy costs, mitigating the risk of floods, making habitats for urban wildlife, tackling air pollution and ","even growing food",".","A 段列好处时包括种植食物。producing 对应 growing；后文北美屋顶菜园是实例，空格问类别 food。"],
      [86,"Doctors are increasingly ","prescribing time spent gardening outdoors"," for patients dealing with anxiety and depression.","B 段医生建议焦虑或抑郁患者在户外园艺。recommends 对应 prescribing，填 gardening；精神问题不是活动名称。"],
      [86,"And research has found that access to even the most basic green spaces can provide a better quality of life for dementia sufferers and ","help people avoid obesity",".","研究称接触绿地有助避免肥胖，同时改善失智患者生活。prevent physical problems 指前者，填 obesity。"],
      [86,"Being able to ","keep enough water at roof height"," and distribute it right across the rooftop is crucial to maintaining the plants on any green roof— especially on 'edible roofs' where fruit and vegetables are farmed.","C。新楼可承重更大，使屋顶储存足量水并分布到各处更容易。题目问容量，不是单位用水是否更省。C、D 顺序不限。"],
      [86,"Having a stronger roof also makes it easier variety of plants, ","since the soil be deeper",".","D。较强的屋顶能承更深土层，因而能栽种更多种类。不涉及生长季更长或横向面积更大。"],
      [87,"There are also combinations of green roofs with solar panels, and 'brown roofs' which are wilder in nature and ","maximise biodiversity",".","A。较野生的棕色屋顶有利于各种生物，maximise biodiversity 对应为多类物种提供栖息地。该双选 A、D 顺序不限。"],
      [87,"There are also ","combinations of green roofs with solar panels",", and 'brown roofs' which are wilder in nature and maximise biodiversity.","D。绿色屋顶结合光伏板，可用可持续来源发电。蓝色屋顶留水更久控制排放速度，文中没说供水给别楼。"],
      [90,"Then, ","in the early 20th century",", progressive thinkers revolted against the notion that inherent ability is destiny.","B。首段由 Binet 等人的先天智力观讲到二十世纪初 Dewey 等的可发展观点，给的是转变发生时间，没有解释学者为何在此时改变。"],
      [90,"A major focus of the growth mindset in schools is coaxing students away from seeing failure as an indication of their ability, and towards ","seeing it as a chance to improve that ability",".","C。学校试图让学生把失败视为改进能力的机会，让他们相信自己能成长。走廊标语和体育人物是做法例子。"],
      [90,"Meanwhile, the former took on only those tasks that ","would not risk their sense of worth",".","D。被夸聪明的一组只选不危及自我评价的任务，怕失败，不肯超出自认能力边界。原文没说他们普遍自尊低。"],
      [90,"The statistician Andrew Gelman claims that 'their research designs have ","enough degrees of freedom"," that they could take their data to support just about any theory at all'.","C 是 Gelman。他批设计自由度太大，研究人员几乎能让同一数据支持任何理论。这就是 methodology 不够严谨。"],
      [91,"In fact, she argues that ","her work has been misunderstood and misapplied"," in a range of ways.","B 是 Dweck。她说自己的工作在多方面被误解和误用。题目考 incorrectly interpreted 与 misunderstood 对应。"],
      [90,"","The concept of intelligence as something innate"," has been supplanted by the idea that intelligence is not fixed, and that, with the right training, we can be the authors of our own cognitive capabilities.","A 是 Binet。首段说他是持早期先天智力观的科学家之一；Dewey 才主张环境能帮助发展智力。"],
      [91,"Growth mindset supporters David Yeager and Gregory Walton claim that interventions should be","delivered in a subtle way"," to maximise their effectiveness.","E 是 Yeager 和 Walton。他们说干预应含蓄，学生若察觉老师认为他们需要帮助，原效果可能被抵消。"],
      [91,"It's ","not just a vehicle for making children feel good",".","B 是 Dweck。她将它定义成学习和进步的工具，并反对与自尊运动混为一谈。feel good 对应 boosting morale。"],
      [91,"He notes that: 'People with a growth mindset don't cope any better with failure Kids with the growth mindset ","aren't getting better grades",", either before or after our intervention study.","D 是 Bates。他尝试复现，结果反复为零，干预前后都未见成绩变好。academic achievement 对应 grades。"],
      [91,"Much of this criticism is not lost on Dweck, and she ","deserves great credit for responding"," to it and adapting her work accordingly.","作者赞扬 Dweck 回应批评并调整研究。deserves great credit 明确表示 admirable，判 YES。"],
      [91,"There is a strong correlation between self-perception and achievement, but there is evidence to suggest that the actual ","effect of achievement on self-perception is stronger"," than the other way round.","作者说实际成就对自我看法的作用更强，题干把两者作用方向颠倒了。演讲成功的例子进一步支持成就驱动信心。"],
      [91,"","Recent evidence would suggest"," that growth mindset interventions are not the elixir of student learning that its proponents claim it to be.","原文评估干预研究和课堂效果，没说媒体怎样报道，更没评价媒体公平性，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [91,"Motivational posters and talks are often a waste of time, and ","might well give students a deluded notion"," of what success actually means.","作者说标语、励志讲话可能让学生误解成功，也质疑直接灌输心态。题干用 may，只说可能有负面效果，判 YES。"],
      [94,"His book on the subject, The Origin of Continents and Oceans, went through four editions and was ","the focus of an international controversy in his lifetime"," and for some years after his death.","Wegener 的书在他生前成为国际争议焦点，widely disputed 对应 international controversy，时间限定也吻合。"],
      [94,"Wegener's basic idea was that many mysteries about the Earth's history could be solved if one supposed that the continents moved laterally, rather than ","supposing that they remained fixed in place",".","传记说明「固定不动」是与大陆漂移相对的假设，但没说有多少著名期刊发表支持文章，判 NOT GIVEN。"],
      [94,"Wegener showed in great detail how such continental movements were plausible and how they worked, using ","evidence from a large number of sciences"," including geology, geophysics, paleontology, and climatology.","地质、地球物理、古生物与气候等均用于论证，large number 与 limited range 直接矛盾，判 NO。"],
      [94,"Plate tectonics is ","in many respects quite different"," from Wegener's proposal, in the same way that modern evolutionary theory is very different from the ideas Charles Darwin proposed in the 1850s about biological …","现代板块构造继承了大陆移动的核心，但很多方面不同。题干说相似性巨大，与作者的明确比较相反，判 NO。"],
      [94,"When I started writing about Wegener's life and work, ","one of the most intriguing things about him for me"," was that, although he came up with a theory on continental drift, he was not a geologist.","I。传记作者从自己的写作视角说最感兴趣的是 Wegener 提漂移理论却并非地质学家。for me 支持 biographer’s perspective。"],
      [94,"He trained as an astronomer and ","pursued a career in atmospheric physics",".","F。此处说他早先的受训及职业方向，提出漂移理论时从事物理和天文教学。摘要空格说 professional interests。"],
      [94,"However, ","he was not an 'unknown","'.","A。1912 年前他已有热气球纪录、受关注考察，还有德国小圈子的名声。已经有人认识，但还不是全面闻名，对应 modest fame。"],
      [94,"In 1906 ","he had set a world record"," (with his brother Kurt) for time aloft in a hot-air balloon: 52 hours.","C。1906 年与兄弟热气球留空 52 小时获世界纪录，六年前且有纪录，恰是 record-breaking achievement。"],
      [94,"Between 1906 and 1908 he had taken part in a highly publicized and ","extremely dangerous expedition"," to the coast of northeast Greenland.","H。1906–1908 年的格陵兰东北海岸考察广为报道但很危险。hazardous 对应 extremely dangerous，exploration 对应 expedition。"],
      [94,"He had also made a name for himself ","amongst a small circle"," of meteorologists and atmospheric physicists in Germany as the author of a textbook, Thermodynamics of the Atmosphere (1911), and of a number of interesting …","E。教材与论文让他在德国气象和大气物理的小圈子出名。a select group 改写 small circle。"],
      [95,"My own feeling, however, is that ","the parts do not make as much sense on their own"," as do all of his activities taken together.","B。索引能帮人查单项，作者仍劝读者串起全部经历，才能理解几次中断、转变和回归。说的是读全书的理由。"],
      [95,"Only a few hundred of the many thousands of letters he wrote and received in his lifetime have survived and he ","didn't keep notebooks or diaries"," that recorded his life and activities.","A。原文还说他很少参加学会，不靠专业关系或政治推观点，多独自研究；选项“不特别有进取心”在这里指不主动追求影响力，而非科研不努力。"],
      [95,"The more such material a scientist leaves behind, ","the better chance a biographer has"," of forming an accurate picture of how a scientist's ideas took shape and evolved.","D。Newton 等留下大量笔记信件，让传记作者较易还原思想怎样成形。作者没比较发表论文的影响大小。"],
      [95,"We plan, think, and act, often with apparent freedom, but most of the time ","our lives 'happen to us","', and we only retrospectively turn this happenstance into a coherent narrative of fulfilled intentions.","C。人虽计划和行动，许多事仍是发生在我们身上的，事后才串起来。末尾区分 Wegener 计划的人生与实际遭遇，支持控制有限。"]
    ]
  ]
};
